      "writtenOn": "2012-09-18T00:10:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I had it initially using do {} while\u0027s but I find they make the code a little harder to read since you can\u0027t tell what the loop is doing until you get to the bottom.  I agree it\u0027s a little nicer looking, but I think it\u0027s probably clearer like this.  If do {} while\u0027s are common here though I\u0027d be happy to change it, I just haven\u0027t ran into many so far.\n\nIt seems like putting it in a function won\u0027t accomplish much, it\u0027s not going to get used anywhere else and it\u0027s not sure long/complex.\n\nI didn\u0027t want to add anything to the lower-level calls for fear of side effects in other parts since we don\u0027t have a ton of time to test stuff here anymore either.  Plus the other systems *should* already handle failed i2c messages.",
